// Lowering from the places IR (0.26.1, docs/design/places-ir.md §2, §8
// step 4): a function's kept body (places/keep.vl) to the IR of ir.vl, in
// place of the AST walk of mod.vl (0.26.2: lower_function, gone).
//
// A local that is scalar and never borrowed whole (the place of an
// RV_REF, with no `*` in it) is an SSA variable; every other local is a
// frame slot (a compound parameter: the caller's copy; a static: its
// address). The CFG is known before the first instruction: one block per
// IR block, lowered in reverse postorder, each sealed once its last
// predecessor is lowered (Braun et al., as mod.vl). Places become address
// arithmetic; an operand is a load, an SSA use or a constant; calls,
// intrinsics and vector operations go through the AST lowering's helpers
// (calls.vl's convention, operand_expr's bindings), checks through
// lower_check. StorageLive and StorageDead are ignored (one slot per
// local, §3.7).
//
// A function is lowered here when its body was kept and every statement
// in it is one this file handles; otherwise mod.vl's AST walk lowers it,
// counted with its reason (lower_stats). An IR-lowered function runs the
// IR's drops and ignores the AST's.

